declare
  v_plan constant jsonb := $audit_plan${"generatedBy":"scripts/audit/apply-audit-fixes.ts","problems":[{"patch_id":"S-01","problem_id":"923bc69f-c8f4-4db2-b71b-222ca8808713","from_version_id":"b2e127c8-30a8-4ba1-92cc-cbb2fbf1e573","expect":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"두 식이 같은 고도를 나타내는 시각을 구하려면 연립방정식을 풀어야 한다. $$\\begin{cases} y = -200x + 6000 \\\\ y = -350x + 9000 \\end{cases}$$ 두 식의 우변을 같게 놓으면 $-200x + 6000 = -350x + 9000$이다. 양변에 $350x$를 더하면 $150x + 6000 = 9000$이고, $6000$을 빼면 $150x = 3000$이므로 $x = 10$이다. 이를 첫 번째 식에 대입하면 $y = -200(10) + 6000 = -2000 + 6000 = 4000$이다. 그래프에서도 직선 $a$와 직선 $b$가 $x=10$ 근처에서 교차하며 그 높이가 $4000$임을 확인할 수 있다. 따라서 정답은 C번이다. 오답 A는 두 식을 계산하는 과정에서 부호를 잘못 처리해 $150x$ 대신 $250x$로 잘못 나눈 경우 나올 수 있는 값이고, 오답 B는 $x=20$일 때 각 직선의 $y$값을 개별적으로 잘못 계산해 나온 값이며(교점이 아님), 오답 D는 두 기울기의 차이를 잘못 계산($150$ 대신 $200$으로 착각)하여 $x=15$로 잘못 구한 경우이다.","explanation_en":"To find the time when the two equations give the same altitude, we solve the system. $$\\begin{cases} y = -200x + 6000 \\\\ y = -350x + 9000 \\end{cases}$$ Setting the right sides equal gives $-200x + 6000 = -350x + 9000$. Adding $350x$ to both sides gives $150x + 6000 = 9000$, and subtracting $6000$ gives $150x = 3000$, so $x = 10$. Substituting this into the first equation gives $y = -200(10) + 6000 = -2000 + 6000 = 4000$. On the graph as well, lines $a$ and $b$ cross near $x=10$ at a height of $4000$. So the answer is C. Wrong answer A could come from mishandling a sign and dividing by $250x$ instead of $150x$. Wrong answer B comes from miscalculating each line's $y$-value separately at $x=20$ (that is not the intersection). Wrong answer D comes from miscalculating the difference of the slopes (mistaking $150$ for $200$) and getting $x=15$."},"set":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"두 식이 같은 고도를 나타내는 시각을 구하려면 연립방정식을 풀어야 한다. $$\\begin{cases} y = -200x + 6000 \\\\ y = -350x + 9000 \\end{cases}$$ 두 식의 우변을 같게 놓으면 $-200x + 6000 = -350x + 9000$이다. 양변에 $350x$를 더하면 $150x + 6000 = 9000$이고, $6000$을 빼면 $150x = 3000$이므로 $x = 20$이다. 이를 첫 번째 식에 대입하면 $y = -200(20) + 6000 = 2000$이고, 두 번째 식에서도 $-350(20) + 9000 = 2000$이므로 두 직선은 $(20, 2000)$에서 만난다. 따라서 정답은 B번이다. 다른 선택지는 두 고도가 서로 다르다(예: $x=10$이면 A기 $4000$, B기 $5500$).","explanation_en":"To find when the two altitudes are equal, set the expressions equal: $-200x + 6000 = -350x + 9000$. Adding $350x$ to both sides gives $150x + 6000 = 9000$, and subtracting $6000$ gives $150x = 3000$, so $x = 20$. Substituting into the first equation gives $y = -200(20) + 6000 = 2000$, and the second equation gives $-350(20) + 9000 = 2000$, so the lines meet at $(20, 2000)$, the right-hand end of the graphed domain. Therefore, the correct answer is B. In the other choices the two altitudes differ at the listed time (for example, at $x = 10$ Airplane A is at $4000$ feet but Airplane B is at $5500$ feet)."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.529Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x 0~20, y 0~9000), 가로축 Time (minutes), 세로축 Altitude (feet). a: y = −200x + 6000; b: y = −350x + 9000."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-01","fromVersionId":"b2e127c8-30a8-4ba1-92cc-cbb2fbf1e573","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-02","problem_id":"892046e9-bd40-4bb4-be75-874398db8483","from_version_id":"33978c61-9396-43ce-84d1-39403d440a90","expect":{"options":["-4","-2","1","4"],"explanation":"다항함수 $g(x) = (x+2)(x-1)(x-4)$의 x절편은 함수값이 0이 되는 x값, 즉 각 인수를 0으로 만드는 값이다. $x+2=0$이면 $x=-2$, $x-1=0$이면 $x=1$, $x-4=0$이면 $x=4$이다. 따라서 x절편은 $x=-2, 1, 4$이다. 선택지 중 이 값에 해당하는 것은 $-2$뿐이다. 그래프에서도 곡선이 $x=-2, 1, 4$에서 x축을 지나는 것을 확인할 수 있다. $-4$는 인수분해된 식에 나타나지 않으므로 x절편이 아니다. 따라서 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"The x-intercepts of the polynomial function $g(x) = (x+2)(x-1)(x-4)$ are the x-values where the function value is 0, that is, the values that make each factor 0. If $x+2=0$, then $x=-2$; if $x-1=0$, then $x=1$; and if $x-4=0$, then $x=4$. So the x-intercepts are $x=-2, 1, 4$. Among the choices, only $-2$ is one of these values. The graph also confirms that the curve crosses the x-axis at $x=-2, 1, 4$. $-4$ does not appear in the factored expression, so it is not an x-intercept. Therefore, the answer is B."},"set":{"options":["-4","-2","2","3"],"explanation":"다항함수 $g(x) = (x+2)(x-1)(x-4)$의 x절편은 각 인수를 0으로 만드는 값 $x=-2, 1, 4$이다. 선택지 중 이 값에 해당하는 것은 $-2$뿐이다. $-4$, $2$, $3$은 $g$의 영점이 아니다($g(-4)=-80$, $g(2)=-8$, $g(3)=-10$). 따라서 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"For the polynomial $g(x) = (x+2)(x-1)(x-4)$, the x-intercepts occur where the function equals zero, i.e., where each factor equals zero: $x=-2$, $x=1$, $x=4$. Among the answer choices only $-2$ is one of these values; $-4$, $2$ and $3$ are not zeros of $g$ (g(-4) = -80, g(2) = -8, g(3) = -10). The graph confirms the curve crosses the x-axis at $x=-2$, $1$ and $4$ only. Therefore, the correct answer is choice B."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.531Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -5~6, y -15~15). g: y = x³ − 3x² − 6x + 8."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-02","fromVersionId":"33978c61-9396-43ce-84d1-39403d440a90","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-03","problem_id":"9bc4e574-ab2f-4144-8882-3974fc684976","from_version_id":"08b093c6-c205-429d-8c18-e1aa4c2f1b93","expect":{"passage":"For all values of $x$ for which the expression is defined,\n$$\\dfrac{6x^2 - 5x - 6}{2x^2 - 7x + 3} \\div \\dfrac{3x^2 + 7x + 2}{x^2 - 9}$$\nis equivalent to which of the following?","explanation":"각 다항식을 인수분해하면 다음과 같다.\n$6x^2-5x-6=(3x+2)(2x-3)$\n$2x^2-7x+3=(2x-1)(x-3)$\n$3x^2+7x+2=(3x+2)(x+2)$\n$x^2-9=(x+3)(x-3)$\n\n나눗셈을 역수의 곱셈으로 바꾸면\n$$\\frac{(3x+2)(2x-3)}{(2x-1)(x-3)}\\times\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{(3x+2)(x+2)}$$\n이다.\n\n분자·분모에서 $(3x+2)$가 약분되고, $(x-3)$도 분자·분모에서 약분된다. 남는 식은\n$$\\frac{(2x-3)(x+3)}{(2x-1)(x+2)}$$\n이므로 정답은 D이다.\n\nA는 $(2x-1)$을 $(x-1)$로 잘못 쓴 오류(즉 $2x^2-7x+3$의 인수분해를 틀리게 한 경우)이다.\nB는 $(x+3)$과 $(x+2)$가 서로 약분된다고 착각하여(실제로는 서로 다른 인수이므로 약분 불가) 과도하게 약분한 오류이다.\nC는 $6x^2-5x-6$의 인수분해에서 부호를 잘못 처리하여 $(3x+2)$ 대신 $(2x+3)$이 남는다고 착각한 오류이다.","explanation_en":"Factoring each polynomial gives the following.\n$6x^2-5x-6=(3x+2)(2x-3)$\n$2x^2-7x+3=(2x-1)(x-3)$\n$3x^2+7x+2=(3x+2)(x+2)$\n$x^2-9=(x+3)(x-3)$\n\nTurning the division into multiplication by the reciprocal gives\n$$\\frac{(3x+2)(2x-3)}{(2x-1)(x-3)}\\times\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{(3x+2)(x+2)}$$\n.\n\n$(3x+2)$ cancels between numerator and denominator, and $(x-3)$ also cancels between numerator and denominator. What remains is\n$$\\frac{(2x-3)(x+3)}{(2x-1)(x+2)}$$\nso the answer is D.\n\nA is an error of writing $(2x-1)$ as $(x-1)$ (that is, factoring $2x^2-7x+3$ incorrectly).\nB is an error of thinking that $(x+3)$ and $(x+2)$ cancel each other (they are different factors and cannot cancel), which is over-cancelling.\nC is an error of mishandling the signs when factoring $6x^2-5x-6$ and thinking that $(2x+3)$ remains instead of $(3x+2)$."},"set":{"passage":"For all values of $x$ for which the expression is defined,\n$$\\dfrac{6x^2 - 5x - 6}{2x^2 - 7x + 3} \\div \\dfrac{3x^2 + 8x + 4}{x^2 - 9}$$\nis equivalent to which of the following?","explanation":"각 다항식을 인수분해하면 다음과 같다.\n$6x^2-5x-6=(3x+2)(2x-3)$\n$2x^2-7x+3=(2x-1)(x-3)$\n$3x^2+8x+4=(3x+2)(x+2)$\n$x^2-9=(x+3)(x-3)$\n\n나눗셈을 역수의 곱셈으로 바꾸면\n$$\\frac{(3x+2)(2x-3)}{(2x-1)(x-3)}\\times\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{(3x+2)(x+2)}$$\n이다.\n\n분자·분모에서 $(3x+2)$가 약분되고, $(x-3)$도 분자·분모에서 약분된다. 남는 식은\n$$\\frac{(2x-3)(x+3)}{(2x-1)(x+2)}$$\n이므로 정답은 D이다.\n\nA는 $(2x-1)$을 $(x-1)$로 잘못 쓴 오류(즉 $2x^2-7x+3$의 인수분해를 틀리게 한 경우)이다.\nB는 $(x+3)$과 $(x+2)$가 서로 약분된다고 착각하여(실제로는 서로 다른 인수이므로 약분 불가) 과도하게 약분한 오류이다.\nC는 $6x^2-5x-6$의 인수분해에서 부호를 잘못 처리하여 $(3x+2)$ 대신 $(2x+3)$이 남는다고 착각한 오류이다.","explanation_en":"Factor each polynomial: $6x^2-5x-6=(3x+2)(2x-3)$, $2x^2-7x+3=(2x-1)(x-3)$, $3x^2+8x+4=(3x+2)(x+2)$ and $x^2-9=(x+3)(x-3)$. Dividing by a fraction is multiplying by its reciprocal: $$\\frac{(3x+2)(2x-3)}{(2x-1)(x-3)}\\times\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{(3x+2)(x+2)}.$$ The factors $(3x+2)$ and $(x-3)$ cancel, leaving $$\\frac{(2x-3)(x+3)}{(2x-1)(x+2)},$$ so the answer is D. Choice A changes $(2x-1)$ to $(x-1)$; B cancels $(x+3)$ against $(x+2)$, which are different factors; C uses $(2x+3)$ instead of $(2x-3)$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.534Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-03","fromVersionId":"08b093c6-c205-429d-8c18-e1aa4c2f1b93","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-04","problem_id":"6dd01c64-176b-4830-8337-4eae6faa8e50","from_version_id":"4c8a290f-702c-4b78-b040-64450140e16a","expect":{"options":["$-3t^2 + 6t - 3$","$t^2 - 2t + 1$","$-3t^2 + 6t + 5$","$-3t^2 - 3$"],"passage":"A square poster has side length $t - 1$ inches, and a square photo with side length $2t - 2$ inches is placed inside it, where t is a positive number large enough for this to make sense.","explanation":"(1) 첫 번째 제곱을 전개한다: $(t - 1)^2 = t^2 - 2t + 1$. (2) 두 번째 제곱을 전개한다: $(2t - 2)^2 = 4t^2 - 8t + 4$. (3) 두 번째 전개식 전체에 뺄셈을 분배해 모든 항의 부호를 바꾼다. (4) $t^2$ 항: 1 - 4 = -3, $t$ 항: -2 - (-8) = 6, 상수항: 1 - 4 = -3 이다. (5) 결과는 $-3t^2 + 6t - 3$ 이다. 따라서 정답은 $-3t^2 + 6t - 3$이다.","explanation_en":"(1) Expand the first square. (2) Expand the second square. (3) Distribute the subtraction over every term of the second expansion. (4) Combine like terms. (5) Write the simplified result. So the answer is $-3t^2 + 6t - 3$."},"set":{"options":["$3t^2 - 6t + 3$","$t^2 - 2t + 1$","$3t^2 - 6t + 5$","$3t^2 + 3$"],"passage":"A square poster has side length $2t - 2$ inches, and a square photo with side length $t - 1$ inches is placed inside it, where t is a positive number large enough for this to make sense.","explanation":"(1) 포스터의 넓이: $(2t - 2)^2 = 4t^2 - 8t + 4$. (2) 사진의 넓이: $(t - 1)^2 = t^2 - 2t + 1$. (3) 덮이지 않은 넓이 = 포스터 − 사진 $= 4t^2 - 8t + 4 - (t^2 - 2t + 1)$. (4) 동류항 정리: $3t^2 - 6t + 3$. 따라서 정답은 $3t^2 - 6t + 3$이다.","explanation_en":"(1) Area of the poster: $(2t-2)^2 = 4t^2 - 8t + 4$. (2) Area of the photo: $(t-1)^2 = t^2 - 2t + 1$. (3) Uncovered area = poster minus photo: $4t^2 - 8t + 4 - (t^2 - 2t + 1)$. (4) Distribute the subtraction over every term and combine like terms: $3t^2 - 6t + 3$. So the answer is $3t^2 - 6t + 3$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.534Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-04","fromVersionId":"4c8a290f-702c-4b78-b040-64450140e16a","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-05","problem_id":"0b94e63d-1d30-4fdb-ad23-2ea8895e0978","from_version_id":"9ea95253-1d21-4d51-8e83-2a944c5957e3","expect":{"question":"What is the value of $x$, other than $x = 3$, for which the height of the water arc equals the height at $x = 1$?"},"set":{"question":"What is the value of $x$, other than $x = 1$, for which the height of the water arc equals the height at $x = 1$?"},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.536Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -1~7, y -2~10), 가로축 Horizontal distance (feet), 세로축 Height (feet). f: y = −2x² + 12x − 10."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-05","fromVersionId":"9ea95253-1d21-4d51-8e83-2a944c5957e3","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-06","problem_id":"7ddfae40-f506-48b2-a2c2-fd8dab606f30","from_version_id":"4deeabbf-0083-4af0-87bd-9191c499e0c4","expect":{"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":30,"min":0,"step":5,"title":"Number of paintings (x)"},"y":{"max":25,"min":0,"step":5,"title":"Number of sculptures (y)"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","intercept":16,"kind":"line","label":"8x + 15y = 240","slope":-0.5333},{"id":"l2","intercept":0,"kind":"line","label":"x = 5","slope":0}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"figure":{"type":"plane","axes":{"x":{"min":0,"max":30,"step":5,"title":"Number of paintings (x)"},"y":{"min":0,"max":25,"step":5,"title":"Number of sculptures (y)"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","kind":"line","slope":-0.5333,"intercept":16,"label":"8x + 15y = 240"},{"id":"l2","kind":"line","label":"x = 5","through":[[5,0],[5,25]]}]},"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.537Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x 0~30, y 0~25), 가로축 Number of paintings (x), 세로축 Number of sculptures (y). 직선 8x + 15y = 240: y = −0.53x + 16; 직선 x = 5: x = 5."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-06","fromVersionId":"4deeabbf-0083-4af0-87bd-9191c499e0c4","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-07","problem_id":"3dfd2cba-99e0-4fd1-a6dc-7770c3637480","from_version_id":"47a34898-3036-4e4e-82e0-dc56ee027ee8","expect":{"options":["$0$","$\\frac{4}{5}$","$\\frac{16}{25}$","$\\frac{5}{4}$"],"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":7,"min":-7,"step":1,"title":"x (feet)"},"y":{"max":6,"min":-1,"step":1,"title":"y (feet)"}},"objects":[{"domain":[-5,5],"fn":"sqrt","id":"arch","kind":"function","label":"arch","params":[0,0,0]},{"id":"beam","intercept":4,"kind":"line","label":"beam","slope":0}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"options":["$0$","$\\frac{4}{5}$","$\\frac{16}{25}$","$\\frac{3}{5}$"],"figure":{"type":"plane","axes":{"x":{"min":-7,"max":7,"step":1,"title":"x (feet)"},"y":{"min":-1,"max":6,"step":1,"title":"y (feet)"}},"objects":[{"id":"arch","kind":"polygon","vertices":[[-5,0],[-4,2.4],[-2.5,3.4641],[0,4],[2.5,3.4641],[4,2.4],[5,0]],"label":"arch"}]},"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.538Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -7~7, y -1~6), 가로축 x (feet), 세로축 y (feet). 다각형 arch: (-5, 0), (-4, 2.4), (-2.5, 3.46), (0, 4), (2.5, 3.46), (4, 2.4), (5, 0)."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-07","fromVersionId":"47a34898-3036-4e4e-82e0-dc56ee027ee8","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-08","problem_id":"0196302d-ba73-42f5-971b-4dc66bdf1641","from_version_id":"d2a7cd19-62df-43d6-ac1b-4bd412c16320","expect":{"figure":{"choices":[{"fitLine":{"intercept":25.4667,"slope":4.4061},"kind":"scatter","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,94],[9,58],[10,60]],"type":"data","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yMax":100,"yMin":0,"yStep":10,"yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)"},{"fitLine":{"intercept":26.1333,"slope":4.103},"kind":"scatter","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,84],[9,58],[10,60]],"type":"data","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yMax":100,"yMin":0,"yStep":10,"yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)"},{"fitLine":{"intercept":26.2,"slope":3.0909},"kind":"scatter","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,18],[7,50],[8,56],[9,58],[10,60]],"type":"data","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yMax":100,"yMin":0,"yStep":10,"yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)"},{"fitLine":{"intercept":32.1333,"slope":1.9394},"kind":"scatter","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,56],[9,27],[10,60]],"type":"data","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yMax":100,"yMin":0,"yStep":10,"yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)"}],"type":"figure_choice"}},"set":{"figure":{"type":"figure_choice","choices":[{"type":"data","kind":"scatter","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,94],[9,58],[10,60]],"fitLine":{"slope":4.4061,"intercept":25.4667},"yMin":0,"yMax":100,"yStep":10},{"type":"data","kind":"scatter","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,84],[9,58],[10,60]],"fitLine":{"slope":4.103,"intercept":26.1333},"yMin":0,"yMax":100,"yStep":10},{"type":"data","kind":"scatter","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,66],[7,50],[8,56],[9,58],[10,60]],"fitLine":{"slope":3.3818,"intercept":29.4},"yMin":0,"yMax":100,"yStep":10},{"type":"data","kind":"scatter","xTitle":"Days observed (days)","yTitle":"Ice thickness (meters)","points":[[1,31],[2,35],[3,38],[4,42],[5,44],[6,45],[7,50],[8,56],[9,27],[10,60]],"fitLine":{"slope":1.9394,"intercept":32.1333},"yMin":0,"yMax":100,"yStep":10}]},"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.541Z","issues":[],"alt":"그래프/도형 선택지 4개(A, B, C, D) — 같은 축·크기로 나란히."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-08","fromVersionId":"d2a7cd19-62df-43d6-ac1b-4bd412c16320","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-09","problem_id":"dc8db05b-3584-4432-82f3-706133bdb691","from_version_id":"d24e2fb8-165b-4da8-863c-3f3b4df0e97b","expect":{"options":["$400 \\cdot (3^{6})^{t}$","$400 \\cdot (3^{1/6})^{t}$","$400 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (t/6)$","$400 \\cdot (1/3)^{-t/6}$"]},"set":{"options":["$400 \\cdot (3^{6})^{t}$","$400 \\cdot (3^{1/6})^{t}$","$400 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (t/6)$","$400 \\cdot (1/3)^{t/6}$"]},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.542Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-09","fromVersionId":"d24e2fb8-165b-4da8-863c-3f3b4df0e97b","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-10","problem_id":"20a54859-dce7-4280-9786-f449da9b72d0","from_version_id":"8cbdc9eb-321e-4614-9f84-0b55fd614fd5","expect":{"passage":"Astronomers tracking the dwarf planet Eris noticed that its surface reflects nearly all incoming sunlight, appearing brighter than expected for a body so far from the sun. ______ its extreme distance, Eris should look dim, but a fresh coating of frozen nitrogen keeps its surface highly reflective.","explanation":"문장은 에리스가 멀리 있어 어두워야 하지만 실제로는 질소 코팅 때문에 밝게 보인다는, 예상과 반대되는 결과를 설명한다. 이는 양보 관계이므로 'Despite'가 정답이다. 나머지 선택지는 모두 원인이나 근거를 나타내는 표현이라 '그런데도 불구하고'라는 문맥과 맞지 않는다.","explanation_en":"The sentence explains an unexpected result: Eris should be dark because it is far away, but it actually looks bright because of its nitrogen coating. This is a concessive relationship, so \"Despite\" is the answer. All the other choices express cause or grounds, so they do not fit the meaning of \"in spite of that.\""},"set":{"passage":"Astronomers tracking the dwarf planet Eris noticed that its surface reflects nearly all incoming sunlight, appearing brighter than expected for a body so far from the sun. ______ its extreme distance, Eris appears bright, thanks to a fresh coating of frozen nitrogen that keeps its surface highly reflective.","explanation":"문장은 에리스가 멀리 있음에도 밝게 보인다는, 예상과 반대되는 사실을 서술한다. 양보 관계이므로 'Despite'가 정답이다. 'Given', 'Because of', 'As a result of'는 거리가 밝음의 원인이라는 뜻이 되어 맞지 않는다.","explanation_en":"The sentence contrasts the expectation set by distance with what is actually observed: Eris is far away, yet it appears bright. A concession is needed, so \"Despite\" is correct. \"Given,\" \"Because of,\" and \"As a result of\" all present the distance as the cause of the brightness, which does not make sense."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.543Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-10","fromVersionId":"8cbdc9eb-321e-4614-9f84-0b55fd614fd5","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-11","problem_id":"209a923d-d40a-4d2a-8c6d-4f291963952f","from_version_id":"02b29ab8-6a50-45c1-acbd-b122f73ae142","expect":{"options":["to have examined","one who examines","examining","an examination that considers"],"explanation":"\"requires\" 뒤에는 동명사가 목적어로 와야 하며, \"examining\"은 이어지는 세 개의 how절을 자연스럽게 목적어로 취한다. \"to have examined\"는 완료부정사로 requires의 목적어 자리에 시제상 불필요하고 어색하며, \"one who examines\"는 사람을 가리키는 명사구로 how절들을 목적어로 받을 수 없고, \"an examination that considers\"는 명사구 뒤에 관계절이 붙는 구조라 이어지는 how절들과 문법적으로 연결되지 않아 동사 뒤에 올바른 형태를 요구하는 규칙을 위반한다.","explanation_en":"After \"requires,\" a gerund must serve as the object, and \"examining\" naturally takes the three following how-clauses as its objects. \"To have examined\" is a perfect infinitive whose tense is unnecessary and awkward in the object position of requires. \"One who examines\" is a noun phrase referring to a person and cannot take how-clauses as objects. \"An examination that considers\" is a noun phrase followed by a relative clause, so it does not connect grammatically to the following how-clauses, which violates the rule requiring the correct form after the verb."},"set":{"options":["to have examined","one who examines","examining","examine"],"explanation":"\"requires\" 뒤에는 동명사가 목적어로 와야 하며 \"examining\"이 뒤의 세 how절을 목적어로 취한다. \"to have examined\", \"one who examines\", \"examine\"은 requires의 목적어 자리에 올 수 없다.","explanation_en":"\"Requires\" takes a gerund as its object, and \"examining\" governs the three following how-clauses. \"To have examined\" (perfect infinitive), \"one who examines\" (a person, not an action), and \"examine\" (a bare verb) cannot serve as the object of \"requires\" here."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.544Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-11","fromVersionId":"02b29ab8-6a50-45c1-acbd-b122f73ae142","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-12","problem_id":"1a7c11c4-a457-435c-a599-6ff1c564868b","from_version_id":"f13adbb6-be49-4477-add4-adce18731d65","expect":{"options":[", which offered","offering","; offering",", offering"],"explanation":"빈칸 앞은 완전한 독립절(Some planners proposed elevated tracks)이고, 빈칸 뒤는 동사가 없는 명사구(a solution that promised...)이다. 이런 비독립적 수식 구는 분사(offering)를 사용해 콤마로 연결하는 것이 표준이므로 D가 정답이다. A는 관계대명사절(which offered)을 쓰지만 동사 offered 앞에 which가 있어도 의미상 괜찮아 보이지만, 뒤에 이어지는 'a solution'이 이미 명사구이므로 which offered a solution 구조가 되어 이중 서술이 되어 어색하다. B는 구두점이 전혀 없어 독립절과 분사구 사이의 경계가 불분명하다. C는 세미콜론 뒤에 독립절이 아닌 분사구가 와서 세미콜론 사용 규칙을 어긴다. 따라서 정답은 D이다.","explanation_en":"What comes before the blank is a complete independent clause (Some planners proposed elevated tracks), and what comes after is a noun phrase with no verb (a solution that promised...). For this kind of dependent modifying phrase, it is standard to use a participle (offering) joined with a comma, so D is the answer. A uses a relative clause (which offered), but it may look fine because the verb offered follows which; since \"a solution\" that follows is already a noun phrase, \"which offered a solution\" creates a double predicate and is awkward. B has no punctuation at all, so the boundary between the independent clause and the participial phrase is unclear. C puts a participial phrase, not an independent clause, after a semicolon, which breaks the rule for using semicolons. So the answer is D."},"set":{"options":[", which offering","offering","; offering",", offering"],"explanation":"빈칸 앞은 완전한 독립절이고 뒤는 명사구이므로 쉼표 + 분사(, offering)로 잇는 D가 맞다. A(which offering)는 관계대명사 뒤에 정동사가 없고, B는 구두점이 없어 경계가 불분명하며, C는 세미콜론 뒤에 독립절이 아닌 구가 와서 틀리다.","explanation_en":"Before the blank is a complete independent clause, and after the blank is a noun phrase (a solution that promised ...). A participle introduced by a comma (\", offering\") correctly attaches that phrase. \"Which offering\" has a relative pronoun without a finite verb, \"offering\" with no punctuation does not mark the boundary, and the semicolon in C cannot precede a non-independent phrase. Therefore, D is correct."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.544Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-12","fromVersionId":"f13adbb6-be49-4477-add4-adce18731d65","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-13","problem_id":"0cf57c09-cb27-4166-9f90-10d260c961e5","from_version_id":"83aee691-a289-4a60-b8db-0af39131ee9c","expect":{"options":["and this launched","they launched","launching","which had launched"],"explanation":"빈칸 앞 절 전체(천문학자들이 이 신호가 지구가 아닌 우주 먼 곳의 사건에서 왔음을 깨달은 것)가 결과적으로 새로운 학문 분야를 \"만들어냈다\"는 의미를 나타내야 하므로, 정동사 없는 분사구 \"launching\"이 앞 절 전체를 의미상 수식하며 결과를 나타내기에 적절하다. \"and this launched\"는 \"this\"가 무엇을 가리키는지 모호하고 등위접속사로 두 절을 나란히 붙여 인과관계를 약화시킨다. \"they launched\"는 \"they\"가 앞 문장의 \"cataclysmic events\"나 \"astronomers\" 중 무엇을 가리키는지 불분명하며 콤마로 독립절을 이어 붙이는 오류를 만든다. \"which had launched\"는 과거완료로 시제가 앞뒤 문맥과 맞지 않고, 관계대명사 \"which\"가 바로 앞의 명사구(\"the solar system\")를 가리키는 것처럼 오독되어 의미가 왜곡된다. 따라서 정답은 C번이다.","explanation_en":"The whole clause before the blank (astronomers realizing that the signal came from an event far out in space rather than from Earth) needs to express the result that it \"created\" a new field of study, so the participial phrase \"launching,\" which has no finite verb, fits well: it modifies the entire preceding clause and expresses the result. \"And this launched\" is ambiguous about what \"this\" refers to, and joining the two clauses with a coordinating conjunction weakens the cause-and-effect relationship. \"They launched\" makes it unclear whether \"they\" refers to \"cataclysmic events\" or \"astronomers,\" and it creates a comma splice by joining independent clauses with a comma. \"Which had launched\" uses the past perfect, which does not match the tense of the surrounding context, and the relative pronoun \"which\" could be misread as referring to the nearest noun phrase (\"the solar system\"), distorting the meaning. Therefore, the answer is C."},"set":{"options":["and this launching","they launched","launching","which had launched"],"explanation":"빈칸 앞 절 전체가 새로운 학문 분야를 만들어냈다는 결과를 나타내야 하므로 정동사 없는 분사구 \"launching\"이 적절하다. \"and this launching\"은 등위접속사 뒤에 정동사가 없고, \"they launched\"는 콤마로 독립절을 이어 붙이며 대명사가 불분명하고, \"which had launched\"는 시제가 맞지 않고 \"the solar system\"을 수식하는 것으로 오독된다. 정답은 C.","explanation_en":"The clause before the blank as a whole needs to be shown as having resulted in a new field of study, so the participial phrase \"launching\" appropriately modifies the entire preceding clause. \"And this launching\" has no finite verb after a coordinating conjunction; \"they launched\" splices two independent clauses with a comma and has an unclear pronoun; \"which had launched\" has a mismatched tense and can be misread as modifying \"the solar system.\" Therefore, C is correct."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T15:54:00.544Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"S-13","fromVersionId":"83aee691-a289-4a60-b8db-0af39131ee9c","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"S-14","problem_id":"